  "indiacall": null,
  "notes": [
    "Detector EERs use the first 4 s of each clip, passed through the named phone channel (ffmpeg codecs).",
    "IndiaCall: teammates' and volunteers' consented voices and the teammates' clones, streamed through the live engine over G.711. Genuine reply delays are sampled from a placeholder distribution (log-normal, median 0.64 s, clipped to 0.3-1.6 s), because data/indiacall/human_lags.json did not exist yet; attacker delays come from the attack model. Audio, words, scoring, policy and passkey signatures are real.",
    "Genuine calls from another number are reported apart from the registered number: the policy gives them a liveness check by design, so they are expected to reach AMBER and are not counted against the 5% target.",
    "Detection only: attacks that spoof the registered number carry no caller-ID flag, so their tier comes from the voice signals alone.",
    "Speakers whose voices were cloned were never in S1 training data.",
    "Phone mic, played through a speaker: \"ota\" channels are simulated (ml/augment/telephony.py over_the_air): a small loudspeaker 15 cm to 1 m from the phone in a synthetic room, room noise, the phone's noise suppressor and AGC, then the codec. Genuine clips in those channels are spoken into the same phone from 3 to 80 cm, without the loudspeaker. ReplayDF rows are real re-recordings in which genuine speech was replayed through the loudspeaker too, so their false alarms are a worst case."
  ]
}